== 4. Does the differentiation axis behave? ==================== 
  basal vs differentiation score: rho = -0.499, p = < 2.2e-16 
  A negative correlation is expected: basal and suprabasal programmes 
  are mutually exclusive in epidermis. If positive, the axis is not 
  capturing differentiation and nothing below should be trusted. 

  axis vs detected genes: rho = +0.017, p = 0.476 
  Differentiated cells detect MORE genes, so part of any rise in 
  RASSF9 detection could be complexity rather than biology. 
  Section 5's complexity-matched column is then the one to read. 

