== 7. Does RASSF9 travel with CDKN1A (p21)? ==================== 
  RASSF9-positive keratinocytes: 172 | negative: 1618 
  CDKN1A detected in 41.86% of RASSF9+ vs 40.05% of RASSF9- cells 
  CDKN1A mean (thinned counts): 12.605 vs 15.433 | Wilcoxon p = 0.914 
 
  CAUTION: CDKN1A also rises with differentiation in its own right, 
  so this comparison cannot separate 'RASSF9 marks p21-high cells' 
  from 'both rise together along the axis'. The model below adds 
  the axis as a covariate to ask whether RASSF9 carries anything 
  beyond it. A null there does NOT refute Lee's mechanism; a 
  co-regulated pair is exactly what his model predicts. 
  p21 ~ RASSF9 + axis + complexity: OR = 0.859, p = 0.380 

== 8. Negative control in melanocytes ========================== 
  RASSF9 is essentially absent from melanocytes (5 of 6,379), so no 
  differentiation gradient should appear here. If one does, the 
  quintile result above is suspect. 
